    {
      "id": "claim_c8fd07d18fb445619cf6a7c00b667d08",
      "statement": "Single node proves each write via the bucket (~90ms for a region-local store); two or more nodes prove a write as soon as a follower holds it on disk (~25ms measured) — so nodes should not be deployed with extra fleet flags (a second node needs no extra configuration because nodes discover each other through bucket leases), the public listener routes Worker ingress while the internal one serves peers/operators on a trusted private network, and the bucket credential must be treated as fleet administration.",
